1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Space missions create a demanding setting for reviewing health observations. CyberNova is an independent research prototype. The crew and telemetry are synthetic.

2
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Activity, source quality and time matter. A missing sensor channel needs a different explanation from a valid signal that changes. Neither establishes a diagnosis.

3
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Six connected views bring together overview metrics, health history, observations, daily check-ins, radiation and research. Demo fixtures stay visibly separate from Live API mode.

4
00:02:45,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Amina’s simulator sends synthetic packets. FastAPI validates units and source fields. SQLite persists records. Statistical observations and source-quality events travel separately to Next.js.

5
00:04:00,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Rolling median and median absolute deviation describe a personal history. EWMA provides trend context. Warm-up, activity separation and persistence rules support engineering observations for human review.

6
00:05:30,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Select fictional crew, explore health history and review source quality. Daily check-ins use fatigue one through seven. Radiation dose rate and accumulated dose remain distinct. Public Vercel uses synthetic Demo fixtures.

7
00:07:00,000 --> 00:08:00,000
NASA Human Research Program resources informed the design. OSDR OSD-53 catalog metadata supplies research context. No experimental gene-expression values or NASA biometric series are analyzed.

8
00:08:00,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Rayane: leadership and integration. Khawla: original backend contribution. Amina: simulator. Ali: analytics prototype and review. Ayoub: scientific references. Fifty-one backend and analytics tests passed in the verified release.

9
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Future work includes suitable governed data, scientific evaluation, security controls and operational usability testing. These are future goals and are not implemented clinical capabilities.

10
00:09:40,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Transparent observations. Visible uncertainty. Human review. CyberNova X. Independent Space Apps project, with no NASA endorsement.
